EKRAN METNİ:
BUNU BİLİYOR MUYDUNUZ?
Süleymaniye Camii'nde Mimar Sinan'ın işlediği bir baykuş figürü var — ve ilginç bir tesadüf: Mimar Sinan Üniversitesi'nin logosu da bir baykuş.

--- VİDEO PROMPT'U ---
@Görsel: [Referans fotoğrafı yükle — mukarnas nişi, her oyma detayı olduğu gibi korunacak, yeniden tasarlanmayacak]

@Video: A slow, reverent dolly-in from a low upward angle, as if a visitor at the mosque threshold is tilting their head back to look up for the first time. The camera glides smoothly toward the vaulted niche, keeping the full owl-like silhouette — the arched "head," the twin star-carved "eyes," the pointed "beak" pendant — entirely within frame throughout, never cropping past its edges. Warm late-afternoon sunlight filters in at a low angle, catching the ridges of the muqarnas stalactites and casting soft, shifting shadows into their hollows. Fine dust motes drift lazily through a single visible shaft of light. The color grade favors rich amber and honey tones deepening into soft charcoal shadow at the edges — an intimate, hushed, almost reverent mood, like the instant just before someone notices a hidden shape in an old carving. No sudden movement, no cuts — one continuous, unhurried breath of a shot. Documentary-cinema realism, shallow atmospheric depth, 9:16 vertical, no text, no logos, no overlays.

EKRAN METNİ:
BUNU BİLİYOR MUYDUNUZ?
Rumeli Hisarı'nın üç kulesi, aralarında bir yarış yaratmak için üç ayrı vezire paylaştırılmış.

--- VİDEO PROMPT'U ---
@Görsel: [Üç kuleyi kapsayan geniş açı bir fotoğraf yükle, varsa]

@Video: A slow, sweeping aerial-style glide along the Bosphorus shoreline, revealing Rumeli Hisarı's three massive stone towers one by one as the camera drifts laterally past the fortress walls at golden hour. Warm late-sun light rakes across the weathered stone, throwing long dramatic shadows between the crenellations; a faint golden haze softens the horizon where the strait meets the sky. As the camera settles, the subtle architectural differences between the three towers become visible — each built in its own hand, its own rhythm of stonework — as if inviting the viewer to notice the "race" once run between them. Ships pass in soft-focus in the background water, adding quiet scale and life. Smooth, unhurried, gliding camera motion throughout, no jarring cuts. Rich amber-gold color grade against deep charcoal stone, cinematic documentary realism, 9:16 vertical, no text, no logos.

EKRAN METNİ:
BUNU BİLİYOR MUYDUNUZ?
Yerebatan Sarnıcı'ndaki ünlü Medusa başlarından biri neden ters duruyor, hâlâ tam olarak bilinmiyor.

--- VİDEO PROMPT'U ---
@Görsel: [Medusa başı sütun kaidesinin gerçek fotoğrafını yükle, orijinal haliyle korunacak]

@Video: A slow, moody dolly-in through the dim, cavernous cistern, moving low over the still black water toward the famous inverted Medusa head at the base of a column. Shafts of dim amber light fall from unseen openings above, catching drifting motes of dust and moisture in the air. The water's surface holds a near-perfect mirror reflection of the carved stone face, rippling almost imperceptibly. As the camera nears, the upside-down orientation of the head becomes the visual focus — deliberately framed to provoke the question of "why." Deep shadow dominates the periphery, forcing the eye toward the lit stone. Hushed, mysterious, cathedral-like atmosphere; slow, deliberate pacing with no sudden movement. Cinematic documentary realism, cool-to-warm contrast (cool ambient shadow, warm highlight on the stone), 9:16 vertical, no text, no logos.

EKRAN METNİ:
BUNU BİLİYOR MUYDUNUZ?
Binbirdirek Sarnıcı'nda 224 sütun var — ama yıllarca "ters duran bir haç" rivayeti daha çok konuşuldu.

--- VİDEO PROMPT'U ---
@Görsel: [Sütun ormanının gerçek fotoğrafını yükle]

@Video: A slow, continuous tracking shot gliding forward through an endless forest of ancient brick columns receding into darkness, evoking the sheer scale implied by "224 columns." Warm, low pinpoint light sources glow at the base of each column, fading to near-total black in the middle distance, creating a rhythmic repetition of light and shadow as the camera advances. Soft haze hangs in the air, catching the light like fine gauze. The camera holds a steady, almost hypnotic forward glide — no side-to-side sway — building a quiet sense of awe and depth. Deep, rich shadow tones with warm amber highlights, cinematic documentary realism, contemplative and slightly eerie mood, 9:16 vertical, no text, no logos.

EKRAN METNİ:
BUNU BİLİYOR MUYDUNUZ?
Yedikule'nin altın kaplı kapısı, fetihten sonra taşlarla örülüp tamamen kapatıldı.

--- VİDEO PROMPT'U ---
@Görsel: [Örülü altın kapı bölümünün gerçek fotoğrafını yükle]

@Video: A slow, deliberate push-in on an ancient stone gate arch, where the eye is drawn to a visibly different, rougher patch of masonry filling what was once an opening — the walled-up remnant of the gate's golden past. Dramatic late-afternoon side light rakes across the wall at a steep angle, exaggerating the seams and texture differences between the original carved stone and the coarser infill blocks, as if the video itself is helping the viewer "read" the wall's history. A single strand of windblown dry grass sways gently in the foreground for scale and life. Warm, sun-baked tones, deep long shadows, slow and unhurried camera movement throughout. Cinematic documentary realism, slightly melancholic and mysterious mood, 9:16 vertical, no text, no logos.

EKRAN METNİ:
BUNU BİLİYOR MUYDUNUZ?
Zeyrek Camii aslında tek yapı değil — üç ayrı kilisenin birleşiminden oluşuyor.

--- VİDEO PROMPT'U ---
@Görsel: [Yapının dış cephesinin farklı bölümlerini gösteren fotoğrafı yükle]

@Video: A slow, wide lateral glide along the exterior of an ancient brick-and-stone building complex, the camera moving steadily enough to reveal — almost like turning pages — the subtle seams and shifts in construction style between what were once three separate structures, now fused into one. Warm afternoon sunlight rakes across the weathered brick, picking out centuries of patched repairs and layered history in the texture. A faint golden dust haze softens the background. Smooth, continuous camera glide, no cuts, building a quiet sense of architectural mystery. Rich warm tones fading to soft shadow, cinematic documentary realism, 9:16 vertical, no text, no logos.

EKRAN METNİ:
BUNU BİLİYOR MUYDUNUZ?
Yoros Kalesi'nin bulunduğu tepe, antik Argonotlar efsanesinde de geçiyor.

--- VİDEO PROMPT'U ---
@Görsel: [Kale ve Boğaz manzarasının fotoğrafını yükle]

@Video: A slow, majestic aerial-style glide rising over an ancient hilltop fortress as the Bosphorus strait unfurls below, ships crossing in miniature in the golden-hour haze. Dramatic clouds catch the last warm light of the day, casting long, shifting shadows across the ruined stone walls. The camera's movement is slow, sweeping, and cinematic — evoking the scale of myth, as if the very hill once watched ancient ships sail the same waters the Argonauts were said to pass. Rich amber-to-violet color grade at the horizon, deep stone shadow in the foreground, cinematic documentary realism, epic and quietly mysterious mood, 9:16 vertical, no text, no logos.

EKRAN METNİ:
BUNU BİLİYOR MUYDUNUZ?
Mihrimah Sultan Camii'nin iki minaresinin, yılda iki kez ekinoks güneşiyle hizalandığı rivayet ediliyor.

--- VİDEO PROMPT'U ---
@Görsel: [Caminin minaresinin gün batımı fotoğrafını yükle]

@Video: A slow, deliberate vertical tilt beginning at the mosque's stone base and rising along the full height of a single slender minaret, silhouetted against a deep golden sunset sky. As the camera ascends, the warm light intensifies toward the top, the minaret's tip catching the last direct rays of the day — a visual echo of the story's claim that the structure aligns precisely with the sun twice a year. Faint wisps of cloud drift slowly across the sky in the background. Smooth, continuous vertical camera movement, no cuts, meditative pacing. Rich gold-to-deep-blue gradient sky, strong architectural silhouette, cinematic documentary realism, 9:16 vertical, no text, no logos.

EKRAN METNİ:
BUNU BİLİYOR MUYDUNUZ?
Fener Rum Patrikhanesi'nin orta kapısı, 1821'den beri hiç açılmadı — 200 yıla yakın süredir kapalı.

--- VİDEO PROMPT'U ---
@Görsel: [Kin Kapısı'nın gerçek fotoğrafını yükle, kapı olduğu gibi korunacak]

@Video: A slow, solemn push-in on an ornate iron gate set into a stone gateway, the gate's surface weathered but its ironwork still intact, closed and undisturbed as if frozen in time. Soft, cool overcast light falls evenly across the metal, with a faint patina of rust and age visible in the grain. A few fallen leaves rest motionless against the base of the gate, untouched, reinforcing the sense of stillness and permanence. The camera moves with quiet, restrained pacing — no dramatic flourish, just a slow, respectful approach, as if paying silent tribute to something long undisturbed. Muted, desaturated color grade with a single warm accent where light catches the ironwork. Cinematic documentary realism, contemplative and solemn mood, 9:16 vertical, no text, no logos.
